LOUP SOURCE-AVAILABLE LICENSE
Version 1.0

Copyright (c) 2026 Code Craft AI LLC

Why this License is strict

The mission of Code Craft AI LLC is to provide trusted-source foundation code
and runtimes: software that others can build on because it is a first-class
product, with a purposely designed revenue stream that funds its maintenance
and development by qualified, trusted engineers.

Loup is a single-source toolchain. Every Loup compiler, interpreter and
runtime comes from Code Craft AI, so that a Loup program behaves the same
wherever it is built and run, and so that the runtime built into every Loup
program can be trusted. The limits this License places on modifying, forking
and distributing the Software exist to protect the integrity of that compiler
and runtime.

If You need something the Software does not provide, You can build it
yourself as a library, package or developer tool (Section 5.3), or propose it
as a feature through the Loup issue tracker or
https://code-craft.ai/contact_us (Section 6).

This preamble explains the purpose of this License. It does not change its
terms.

1. Definitions

- "Licensor" means Code Craft AI LLC.
- "Software" means the Loup language toolchain, compilers, runtimes,
  standard libraries, tools and documentation that Licensor makes available
  under this License, in source or binary form, including updates.
- "Official Build" means a binary distribution of the Software built and
  published by Licensor. Licensor is the only source of Official Builds.
- "You" means the individual or Legal Entity accepting this License. An
  individual accepting on behalf of a Legal Entity binds that entity.
- "Legal Entity" means a company, partnership, sole proprietorship,
  government body, nonprofit or other organization, together with any entity
  it controls. A parent company and its subsidiaries count as one Legal
  Entity.
- "Personal Use" means use by an individual, on their own time and
  equipment, for purposes that do not generate revenue or serve the business
  of any Legal Entity, including their employer, clients or customers.
- "Educational Use" means use by students and instructors for coursework,
  teaching and academic research at an accredited educational institution,
  and use in non-commercial training materials.
- "Commercial Use" means any use that is not Personal Use, Educational Use,
  Open-Source Use or Nonprofit Use. This includes any use on behalf of an
  employer, client or customer; building, maintaining or testing software or
  services that are sold, licensed, hosted or used internally by a business;
  and paid consulting or contract work.
- "Developer" means an individual human who writes, modifies, reviews or
  builds Loup source code, or operates the Software, for Commercial Use.
- "Agent" means an AI system or other automated process that autonomously
  writes, modifies or generates Loup source code for Commercial Use. Build
  servers and CI pipelines that only compile, test or package code written
  by licensed Developers or Agents are not Agents.
- "Seat" means one Commercial License entitlement covering one named
  Developer or one Agent account, for one Term.
- "Your Programs" means software You create using the Software, including
  compiled binaries, scripts and web output, and any Loup runtime or library
  code the Software embeds or links into them.
- "Extensions" means the libraries, packages and developer tools You create
  for the Loup ecosystem, as Section 5.3 describes.
- "Open-Source Use" means developing software that is publicly released,
  with its source code, under a license approved by the Open Source
  Initiative. Software that a Legal Entity, other than a nonprofit, produces
  or maintains for its own purposes, or uses in its own business, is
  commercial code: developing or maintaining it is Commercial Use, even when
  it is publicly released under such a license.
- "Nonprofit Use" means use by, and for the purposes of, an organization
  recognized as tax-exempt nonprofit under the law of its jurisdiction, such
  as a U.S. 501(c)(3) organization.
- "Term" means the five-year period starting on the date a Seat is purchased
  or last renewed.

2. Free License for Personal, Educational, Open-Source and Nonprofit Use

Personal Use, Educational Use, Open-Source Use and Nonprofit Use are free of
charge. Subject to this License, Licensor grants You a worldwide, non-
exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free license to view and inspect the
source code of the Software, to build the Software from its unmodified source
code as Section 5.1 allows, to install and run Official Builds and those
builds, and to create, build and run Your Programs and Extensions, solely for
those uses.

2.1 No work use. A Personal Use license never covers Commercial Use. You may
not use a personally licensed copy for an employer, client or customer,
including outside working hours or on personal equipment. That work requires
a Commercial License held by, or bought for, that Legal Entity.

2.2 Changing purpose. Once You earn income from a program that began as
Personal Use or Educational Use, its development becomes Commercial Use. To
remain compliant, You must buy a Commercial License, with a Seat for each
Developer and Agent working on it, before continuing that development.

3. Commercial License

3.1 Seats. Commercial Use requires a Commercial License with one Seat for
each Developer and each Agent engaged in that use. A Commercial License grants
the same rights as Section 2, for Commercial Use, to the Developers and Agents
it covers.

3.2 Purchase. Seats are purchased from Licensor at
https://code-craft.ai/loup/license. Organizations needing volume or custom
terms may negotiate a bulk license with Licensor through
https://code-craft.ai/contact_us. Where a signed bulk agreement conflicts with
this License, the bulk agreement governs.

3.3 Term. Each Seat covers one Term, starting on the date it is purchased or
last renewed.

3.4 Assigning Seats. A Seat is assigned to one named Developer or one Agent
account at a time. You may reassign a Seat permanently when its Developer
leaves Your organization or stops doing Commercial Use for You, or when an
Agent account is retired. You may not share a Seat or rotate it among
Developers or Agents.

3.5 End of Term. When a Seat's Term ends without renewal, the Developer or
Agent it covered must stop Commercial Use of the Software. Your Programs
built and distributed while the Seat was in effect remain licensed under
Section 4, and their users keep their rights under Section 4.3.

3.6 Compliance. On Licensor's written request, no more than once a year, You
will confirm in writing that the number of Developers and Agents engaged in
Commercial Use does not exceed the Seats You hold.

4. Your Programs

4.1 Ownership. You own Your Programs. This License claims no rights in the
code You write.

4.2 Runtime redistribution. You may freely copy, distribute, sell and
sublicense the Loup runtime and library code that the Software embeds or
links into Your Programs, without royalty, provided Your Programs were built
with a copy of the Software that is properly licensed to You under this
License, whether under the free license (Section 2) or a Commercial License
(Section 3). This permission covers that code only as part of Your Programs.
It does not cover distributing it on its own, or as part of a compiler,
interpreter or runtime that competes with the Software. You may not modify
that code. That code stays under this License even when Your Programs are
distributed under a different license, including an open-source license. The
Loup runtime and library code are a compiler runtime component: they are
included in the normal packaging of the Software's compiler, separately from
the compiler itself, and serve only to enable programs built with the
Software to run.

4.3 Users of Your Programs. No license from Licensor is needed to run, use or
receive Your Programs. Where Your Programs offer scripting or extension in
Loup, built on runtime code You distribute under Section 4.2, their users may
write, run and share scripts for Your Programs through that scripting support
without a license from Licensor, including for commercial purposes, despite
the definition of Commercial Use in Section 1. This permission covers only
scripting performed through Your Programs. Developing Loup software with the
Software itself, outside Your Programs, remains subject to Sections 2 and 3.

5. Source Code, Forks and Extensions

5.1 Source code. Licensor makes the Software's source code available so You
can inspect it and build the Software from it. You may read and study it,
refer to it while creating Your Programs and Extensions, and build the
Software from the unmodified source code for Your own use under this License.
You may not modify it, create derivative works of it, or copy any part of it
into other software, except as a signed Contributor License Agreement with
Licensor permits.

5.2 No forks. You may not create, use or distribute a fork, port, modified
build or derivative of any compiler, interpreter, runtime, standard library
or tool in the Software, except as a signed Contributor License Agreement with
Licensor permits for preparing Contributions. Every compiler, interpreter and
runtime for the Loup language must originate from Licensor.

5.3 Extensions. You may build and distribute, under licenses of Your choosing:

(a) libraries and packages that extend the Loup ecosystem; and

(b) developer tools for Loup, such as editors, editor plugins, language
servers, linters, formatters and debuggers, provided they do not themselves
interpret, execute, compile, transpile or translate Loup code. Such a tool may
run or compile Loup code only by invoking the Software through the interfaces
Licensor provides for that purpose.

An Extension may not include or be derived from the Software's source code.

5.4 Copies and distribution. You may install and run copies of Official
Builds, and of builds You made under Section 5.1, on systems You control,
including build servers and CI images used only within Your organization.
Builds You made under Section 5.1 may never be released or distributed. Any
other distribution of the Software, in source or binary form, to anyone
outside Your organization, including copies of Official Builds, container
images, mirrors and package-manager packages, requires a separate written
Distribution License from Licensor, which states who may distribute the
Software and to whom. Distribution Licenses are requested through
https://code-craft.ai/contact_us.

