6.3 Authority. You confirm that You have the right to make each Contribution,
including any permission required from Your employer.

6.4 What is not a Contribution. Your Programs and Extensions are not
Contributions unless You submit them to Licensor for inclusion in the
Software.

6.5 Contributor License Agreement. Licensor accepts code and documentation
Contributions only from contributors who have signed Licensor's Contributor
License Agreement. Where that agreement and this Section 6 differ, the
Contributor License Agreement governs.

7. Trademarks

7.1 Loup™ and Code Craft AI are trademarks of Code Craft AI LLC. This License
grants no right to use them except as Sections 7.2 to 7.4 allow.

7.2 "Compiled by Loup". You may state that Your Programs were "Compiled by
Loup" if:

(a) the Software was the only compiler used to build them, and the copy used
was properly licensed to You under this License. Tools that the Software
itself runs as part of its build pipeline, such as its LLVM, assembler and
linker stages, count as part of the Software; and

(b) they contain no code written in a language other than Loup, apart from
code that the Software itself generates, embeds or links into the programs it
builds, such as the Loup runtime, the Loup standard library, generated host
glue and the system libraries the Software links by default.

7.3 "Contains Loup code". If Your Programs do not meet Section 7.2, for
example because they also contain code in another language or built by
another compiler, You may state that they "Contain Loup code", provided the
Loup portions were built with a copy of the Software properly licensed to You
under this License.

7.4 Conditions for both statements. You may make the statements in Sections
7.2 and 7.3 in Your Programs and in their documentation, packaging and
marketing, provided that:

(a) the statement is accurate;

(b) You use the words in plain text, and not the Loup logo or other Code
Craft AI artwork, unless Code Craft AI has approved that use in writing;

(c) the statement does not suggest that Code Craft AI sponsors, endorses or
certifies Your Programs; and

(d) You do not use "Loup", or a confusingly similar name, as the name of Your
product, company or web domain, or of any compiler, interpreter or runtime.

8. Termination

8.1 Breach. If You breach this License, Licensor may notify You. If You cure
the breach within 30 days of that notice, Your license continues. If You do
not, Your license ends automatically. A breach of Section 5, or a second
breach of the same kind, ends Your license on notice, with no cure period.

8.2 Patent claims. If You start a lawsuit or other proceeding alleging that
the Software infringes a patent, Your license under this License ends on the
date You start it.

8.3 Effect. When Your license ends, You must stop using the Software and
delete all copies of it in Your possession or control. Copies of Your
Programs distributed before Your license ended remain licensed under Section
4.2, and their users keep their rights under Section 4.3. Ending a license
does not entitle You to a refund of fees already paid.

8.4 Survival. Sections 1, 4.1, 4.3, 6, 7.1, 8.3, 8.4, 9, 10, 11 and 12
survive the end of this License.

